# Calculators and the spreadsheets.

shot    loan
cap     The amortisation calculator.  Principal, term, rate and starting
cap     month in; the payment, the total interest and a month-by-month
cap     schedule out, with a subtotal at each year.  It is fed from a file
cap     here and its report caught in another, because on a terminal the
cap     schedule scrolls thirty years past before you can read the top of
cap     it.  120,000 over thirty years at 6.5% is 758.48 a month.
run     { echo 120000; echo 30; echo 6.5; echo 8; echo s; } > /dd/tmp/la
wait    3
run     loan < /dd/tmp/la > /dd/tmp/lo.txt
wait    10
run     head -n 16 /dd/tmp/lo.txt 2>/nil
wait    6

shot    oleo
cap     GNU Oleo 1.6 does not run: an illegal instruction at 000465d2 and
cap     the process is aborted before it draws a cell.  The three lines
cap     below it are the keystrokes meant for the spreadsheet, landing in
cap     the shell instead.  `sc' is the spreadsheet that works.
run     oleo
wait    4
send    12\r
wait    1
send    30\r
wait    1
send    =A0+A1\r
wait    3
quit    \030\003

shot    rechne
cap     rechne, DESIGNA's German command-line calculator: every answer in
cap     decimal, hex and binary at once.  The expression is ONE argument
cap     with no spaces in it -- 4095+1, 12x12, $ff+1 -- and x multiplies,
cap     m is modulo.  Spaced out, it evaluates each word on its own.
run     rechne 4095+1
wait    2
run     rechne 12x12
wait    2
run     rechne \$ff+1
wait    2
run     rechne 100m7
wait    2
run     rechne -b 12345
wait    3

shot    rpn
cap     An RPN calculator, and the screen shows it going wrong: 12 and 34
cap     push correctly, and then `+' PUSHES A ZERO instead of replacing
cap     them with 46.  The stack grows where it should shrink.
run     rpn
wait    2
send    12\r
wait    1
send    34\r
wait    1
send    +\r
wait    1
send    2\r
wait    1
send    q\r
wait    2


shot    gcl
for     gcl scqref
cap     gcl, a general calculation utility, and scqref -- the quick
cap     reference card for `sc', which is a document rather than a
cap     program and prints itself.
run     scqref | head -n 16
wait    12
run     gcl < /nil
wait    10
